":"Secondary data is data that:","options":["Is freshly collected from the field","Was collected by another party for a different purpose","Is only available through government databases","Consists only of quantitative information"],"correctOption":1,"section":"Basic Concepts & Data Collection"}},{"itemId":"4ca76d32-0dfc-5792-8271-fc57bbd06e99","courseId":"40000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003","kind":"cbt_question","questionId":"6ff3cd0a-5cad-41dc-a10a-4af9baf79989","sourceKey":"quiz:197","parentItemId":null,"revision":1,"payload":{"prompt":"In business research, a 'population' refers to:","options":["Only the human beings being studied","The total collection of all elements about which information is sought","A portion of a larger group selected for study","Only numerical data in a given study"],"correctOption":1,"section":"Statistical Terminology"}},{"itemId":"f011ab2b-8f8b-56bb-8544-e8b9c4af8811","courseId":"40000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003","kind":"cbt_question","questionId":"890b5e74-75a4-44fa-850a-5b27ef120ed5","sourceKey":"quiz:198","parentItemId":null,"revision":1,"payload":{"prompt":"Which of the following is an example of qualitative data?","options":["Height of employees","Monthly revenue figures","Brand preference of consumers","Number of units sold"],"correctOption":2,"section":"Statistical Terminology"}},{"itemId":"e25c27a1-4b0d-5927-bc70-236581b15d31","courseId":"40000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003","kind":"cbt_question","questionId":"b163b709-a730-420f-b056-7544eb72aecc","sourceKey":"quiz:199","parentItemId":null,"revision":1,"payload":{"prompt":"A census differs from a sample survey in that it:","options":["Uses statistical inference","Collects data from every member of the population","Only applies to small groups","Provides estimates rather than exact values"],"correctOption":1,"section":"Basic Concepts & Data Collection"}},{"itemId":"b379f051-dd23-53db-b018-55d991d300c4","courseId":"40000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003","kind":"cbt_question"