les and Concepts"}},{"itemId":"e6712216-8089-5136-9059-12701891453d","courseId":"40000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000015","kind":"cbt_question","questionId":"dd49d23d-1a29-44c6-a3f5-4b65a964b97a","sourceKey":"quiz:82","parentItemId":null,"revision":1,"payload":{"prompt":"Which of the following is one of the stated principles of the circular economy?","options":["Guides government and businesses in environmental planning","To keep products and materials in use","Improve environmental performance","It improves resource efficiency"],"correctOption":1,"section":"Topic 2 — Environmental Principles and Concepts"}},{"itemId":"5d4856a0-6289-5aa3-b571-d312e53c3b3d","courseId":"40000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000015","kind":"cbt_question","questionId":"a49c4cd2-a3e9-40b7-9dd3-60ade19b97dd","sourceKey":"quiz:83","parentItemId":null,"revision":1,"payload":{"prompt":"Which of the following is one of the stated benefits of the circular economy?","options":["It conserves natural resources","Grazing land for livestock","Improves access to environmentally conscious investors and customers","Hazardous substance regulation"],"correctOption":0,"section":"Topic 2 — Environmental Principles and Concepts"}},{"itemId":"43b1d0c7-e200-59da-a143-710667cfaaa5","courseId":"40000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000015","kind":"cbt_question","questionId":"bc6fb469-febe-4a1a-8234-10113fc50e8f","sourceKey":"quiz:84","parentItemId":null,"revision":1,"payload":{"prompt":"Which of the following is one of the stated types of waste?","options":["Industrial waste — waste produced by manufacturing and industrial processing","It reduces production cost","Enhances competitiveness in domestic and international markets","Promote efficient use of resources"],"correctOption":0,"section":"Topic 2 — Environmental Principles and Concepts"}},{"itemId":"7f4d6674-f4bd-55ec-9400-49682de70cdf","courseId":"40000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000015","kind":"cbt_question","questionId":"894f067e-bd0b-47f7-a66d-c3dd990dcaaf","sourceKey":"quiz:85","parentItemId":null,"revision":1,"payload":{"prompt":"Which of the following is one of the stated waste management hierarchy?","options":["Enhances competitiveness in domestic and international markets","Consumption patterns","Re-use — using a product multiple times without significant processing","Water quality regulation"],"correctOption":2,"section":"Topic 2 — Environmental Principles and Concepts"}},{"itemId":"02f676b1-de7d-5aef-9a3b-61727a7b3e07","courseId":"40000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000015","kind":"cbt_question","questionId":"647affe7-db59-4b04-ac50-479a7c941a77","sourceKey":"quiz:86","parentItemId":null,"revision":1,"payload":{"prompt":"Which of the following is one of the stated waste management strategies?","options":["Measures contribution to climate change","Reduce air travel","Separate waste at the source","Improves energy and resource efficiency"],"correctOption":2,"section":"Topic 2 — Environmental Principles and Concepts"}},{"itemId":"cf4a03af-4eee-5375-bc76-1723fde845f7","courseId":"40000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000015","kind":"cbt_question","questionId":"770953bb-6203-41ff-b61a-bcd3bbcda1f4","sourceKey":"quiz:87","parentItemId":null,"revision":1,"payload":{"prompt":"Which of the following is one of the stated relationship between the circular economy and waste management?","options":["Reducing landfill waste","Choose sustainable transportation","Protects natural ecosystems","Supports carbon reduction strategy"],"correctOption":0,"section":"Topic 2 — Environmental Principles and Concepts"}},{"itemId":"8083130e-efac-5c54-894f-348b248a00a3","courseId":"40000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000015","kind":"cbt_question","questionId":"c4a1f513-37c5-468f-9743-1f2a749341e1","sourceKey":"quiz:88","parentItemId":null,"revision":1,"payload":{"prompt":"Which of the following is one of the stated challenges of implementing the circular economy?","options":["Prevention — avoiding or reducing the creation of waste in the first place","Limited recycling infrastructure in some sub-regions","Air quality regulation","Encouraging recycling and remanufacturing"],"correctOption":1,"section":"Topic 2 — Environmental Principles and Concepts"}},{"itemId":"4ccf0c68-d38e-563f-abf5-b6c08050b73f","courseId":"40000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000015","kind":"cbt_question","questionId":"78f5df5f-528d-4f2e-b9ed-d7011e156ed0","sourceKey":"quiz:89","parentItemId":null,"revision":1,"payload":{"prompt":"Which of the following is one of the stated importance of the circular economy for business?","options":["Air quality regulation","Low public awareness and participation","Reduce the use of single-use products","Improves brand reputation and customer trust"],"correctOption":3,"section":"Topic 2 — Environmental Principles and Concepts"}},{"itemId":"90dfd6ad-4d95-5d08-a9d9-36d7637c98cf","courseId":"40000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000015","kind":"cbt_question","questionId":"7a46273a-5358-43f3-9ce7-dd04d0b14f61","sourceKey":"quiz:9","parentItemId":null,"revision":1,"payload":{"prompt":"Which of the following is one of the stated benefits of green management to the organization?","options":["Technological advancement","Cost Savings and Efficiency — eco-friendly practices reduce energy consumption and waste management costs","It enhances corporate reputation and brand loyalty","Improved corporate reputation"],"correctOption":3,"section":"Topic 1 — Introduction to Green Management"}},{"itemId":"b5191082-ec85-5608-97a2-115e78500eb9","courseId":"40000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000015","kind":"cbt_question","questionId":"79f6e0da-04dc-4828-9921-c03b78537e57","sourceKey":"quiz:90","parentItemId":null,"revision":1,"payload":{"prompt":"Which of the following is one of the stated objectives of environmental regulations?","options":["Built-up land for housing and infrastructure","Control pollution and waste","Measures human demand on natural resources","Strengthens brand image and customer trust"],"correctOption":1,"section":"Topic 2 — Environmental Principles and Concepts"}},{"itemId":"6dfba255-7e0c-5a92-b6b3-a72695912872","courseId":"40000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000015","kind":"cbt_question","questionId":"c9046ab8-172d-40cb-9318-6aac6402d4d9","sourceKey":"quiz:91","parentItemId":null,"revision":1,"payload":{"prompt":"Which of the following is one of the stated types of environmental regulation?","options":["Hazardous waste — waste containing substances harmful to human health and the environment, e.g. chemicals","Diet and food choices","Consumption patterns","Water quality regulation"],"correctOption":3,"section":"Topic 2 — Environmental Principles and Concepts"}},{"itemId":"c8a65926-da70-5fac-8c23-787a87e843c7","courseId":"40000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000015","kind":"cbt_question","questionId":"8066c262-11f7-468d-a219-fa4fee4142b4","sourceKey":"quiz:92","parentItemId":null,"revision":1,"payload":{"prompt":"Which of the following is one of the stated objectives of environmental standards?","options":["Municipal waste — household and commercial waste including food scraps, paper, plastics, and glass","Measures contribution to climate change","Encourage continuous improvement","Strengthens brand image and customer trust"],"correctOption":2,"section":"Topic 2 — Environmental Principles and Concepts"}},{"itemId":"ffb4979a-356c-5e47-aac9-557f4df5d78e","courseId":"40000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000015","kind":"cbt_question","questionId":"0e307419-110c-4433-a978-10306114e387","sourceKey":"quiz:93","parentItemId":null,"revision":1,"payload":{"prompt":"Which of the following is NOT one of the stated challenges of implementing the circular economy?","options":["Low public awareness and participation","Inconsistent environmental regulations (bylaws)","Market demand for recycled material may fluctuate","Reduce air travel"],"correctOption":3,"section":"Topic 2 — Environmental Principles and Concepts"}},{"itemId":"7de6a806-a292-5d37-9ac4-bca69431aec8","courseId":"40000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000015","kind":"cbt_question","questionId":"5b8148b4-3121-4c59-b182-298590c11524","sourceKey":"quiz:94","parentItemId":null,"revision":1,"payload":{"prompt":"Which of the following is NOT one of the stated ways to reduce ecological footprint?","options":["Use renewable energy","Reduce food waste","Reduce, reuse, and recycle materials","Air quality regulation"],"correctOption":3,"section":"Topic 2 — Environmental Principles and Concepts"}},{"itemId":"c8dccd89-96a0-5594-9193-1c6a95a2ac6b","courseId":"40000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000015","kind":"cbt_question","questionId":"05dd684a-3a71-4cec-9cb5-1111783c2aea","sourceKey":"quiz:95","parentItemId":null,"revision":1,"payload":{"prompt":"Which of the following is NOT one of the stated importance of measuring ecological footprint?","options":["Raises awareness about sustainable living","Supporting sustainable production and consumption","Measures human demand on natural resources","Assesses whether resource use is sustainable"],"correctOption":1,"section":"Topic 2 — Environmental Principles and Concepts"}},{"itemId":"8657ce12-6d8d-583a-819f-0fb9962045f4","courseId":"40000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000015","kind":"cbt_question","questionId":"60a41542-8a23-4ede-ba2b-9561661151e2","sourceKey":"quiz:96","parentItemId":null,"revision":1,"payload":{"prompt":"Which of the following is NOT one of the stated waste management hierarchy?","options":["Recovery — recovering energy or useful materials from waste that cannot be recycled","Disposal — safely disposing of waste in landfills or through controlled incineration, as a last resort","Protect biodiversity and ecosystems","Recycling — converting waste materials into new products"],"correctOption":2,"section":"Topic 2 — Environmental Principles and Concepts"}},{"itemId":"ae89b24a-de0d-5cbb-8008-d63dca2dfaf7","courseId":"40000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000015","kind":"cbt_question","questionId":"2ff5ef4e-0a58-4a51-acfa-9133c629105f","sourceKey":"quiz:97","parentItemId":null,"revision":1,"payload":{"prompt":"Which of the following is NOT one of the stated components of ecological footprint?","options":["The forest area needed to absorb carbon dioxide emissions","Fishing grounds","Improves public health and safety","Cropland for food production"],"correctOption":2,"section":"Topic 2 — Environmental Principles and Concepts"}},{"itemId":"ad6b6d63-1463-5689-8021-aed852382ed7","courseId":"40000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000015","kind":"cbt_question","questionId":"5c4417f5-daf4-460f-9ed4-5ea101980b64","sourceKey":"quiz:98","parentItemId":null,"revision":1,"payload":{"prompt":"Which of the following is NOT one of the stated differences between environmental regulations and environmental standards?","options":["Environmental regulation has to do with compliance required by law, while standards are often adopted to improve performance and demonstrate best practice","Environmental regulations are legally enforceable rules established by the government, while environmental standards are voluntary or mandatory technical guidelines or management frameworks","Limited technical expertise","Under environmental regulation, non-compliance means the organization must pay a fine; under standards, non-compliance is addressed through improvement rather than legal penalty"],"correctOption":2,"section":"Topic 2 — Environmental Principles and Concepts"}},{"itemId":"abae5dc2-2c80-5d6d-a196-d07d3122d719","courseId":"40000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000015","kind":"cbt_question","questionId":"68a4db96-8022-4a2c-ae06-93492a001420","sourceKey":"quiz:99","parentItemId":null,"revision":1,"payload":{"prompt":"Which of the following is NOT one of the stated challenges of implementing the circular economy?","options":["Low public awareness and participation","Supporting sustainable production and consumption","Complex product designs that are difficult to repair or redesign","Inconsistent environmental regulations (bylaws)"],"correctOption":1,"section":"Topic 2 — Environmental Principles and Concepts"}}]$expected_content$::jsonb,
