f-1f2c-50b9-af24-01aed5ad3cc2","courseId":"e6ebc3e3-e990-5459-84af-06a4f05aea89","kind":"theory_question","questionId":null,"sourceKey":"guide-theory:5","parentItemId":null,"revision":1,"payload":{"prompt":"A Lagos print shop makes branded T-shirts with fixed costs of ₦240,000, variable cost ₦900 per shirt and price ₦1,500. Find the break-even quantity, the break-even revenue and the profit on 500 shirts."}},{"itemId":"09721817-1dac-5dce-8e8d-9bf794e1016b","courseId":"e6ebc3e3-e990-5459-84af-06a4f05aea89","kind":"theory_question","questionId":null,"sourceKey":"guide-theory:6","parentItemId":null,"revision":1,"payload":{"prompt":"A bank lends ₦100,000 as a mortgage repaid by equal monthly payments over 5 years at 6% compounded monthly. Find the monthly payment and the total interest."}},{"itemId":"9d97860a-e6b4-5238-930a-9a2bfe32f3be","courseId":"e6ebc3e3-e990-5459-84af-06a4f05aea89","kind":"theory_question","questionId":null,"sourceKey":"guide-theory:7","parentItemId":null,"revision":1,"payload":{"prompt":"Solve by Cramer's rule: 2x + 5y = 24; 3x + 8y = 38."}},{"itemId":"da4f50e2-430a-554d-963f-b76a46c4bd58","courseId":"e6ebc3e3-e990-5459-84af-06a4f05aea89","kind":"theory_question","questionId":null,"sourceKey":"guide-theory:8","parentItemId":null,"revision":1,"payload":{"prompt":"The 3rd term of a geometric progression is 18 and the 6th term is 486. Find the first term, the common ratio and the sum of the first 5 terms."}},{"itemId":"32f8ea69-0d56-5fd0-a451-38fc24d6aa63","courseId":"e6ebc3e3-e990-5459-84af-06a4f05aea89","kind":"theory_question","questionId":null,"sourceKey":"guide-theory:9","parentItemId":null,"revision":1,"payload":{"prompt":"In a survey of 200 traders, 120 sell rice (R), 90 sell beans (B) and 30 sell both. How many sell neither, and how many sell exactly one item?"}}]$expected_content$::jsonb,
  'mathematics-business: theory_question published payload and identity match source');
select ok((select coalesce(jsonb_agg(jsonb_build_object(
  'itemId', item_id, 'courseId', course_id, 'kind', kind,
  'questionId', question_id, 'sourceKey', source_key,
  'parentItemId', parent_item_id, 'revision', revision,
  'payload', payload) order by source_key collate "C"), '[]'::jsonb)
  from public.read_published_managed_content('e6ebc3e3-e990-5459-84af-06a4f05aea89')
  where kind = 'model_answer') = $expected_content$[{"itemId":"817101dc-f742-5445-b938-e7ccfcc59f4d","courseId":"e6ebc3e3-e990-5459-84af-06a4f05aea89","kind":"model_answer","questionId":null,"sourceKey":"guide-answer:1","parentItemId":"7c5f1877-bd7e-5928-be0b-41285fe8de6f","revision":1,"payload":{"body":"C(x) = ∫ (3x^2 − 4x + 5) dx = x^3 − 2x^2 + 5x + k. At x = 0, C = k = 200 (fixed cost). So C(x) = x^3 − 2x^2 + 5x + 200. C(10) = 1000 − 200 + 50 + 200 = ₦1,050."}},{"itemId":"7f32b7ea-56eb-57da-b229-a008a976443e","courseId":"e6ebc3e3-e990-5459-84af-06a4f05aea89","kind":"model_answer","questionId":null,"sourceKey":"guide-answer:10","parentItemId":"9479ba27-1464-5f19-a0cf-5374cc3c048d","revision":1,"payload":{"body":"• S = ∫ (0.2 − 0.1Y^(−1/2)) dY = 0.2Y − 0.1 × Y^(1/2)/(1/2) + k = 0.2Y − 0.2Y^(1/2) + k.\n• At Y = 25: 0.2(25) − 0.2(5) + k = 0, so 5 − 1 + k = 0 and k = −4. Hence S = 0.2Y − 0.2sqrt(Y) − 4.\n• C = Y − S = Y − 0.2Y + 0.2sqrt(Y) + 4 = 0.8Y + 0.2sqrt(Y) + 4.\n• Check: MPC = 0.8 + 0.1Y^(−1/2), and MPC + MPS = 1."}},{"itemId":"89053ff5-e62a-5862-ae68-29dbb5a17ba9","courseId":"e6ebc3e3-e990-5459-84af-06a4f05aea89","kind":"model_answer","questionId":null,"sourceKey":"guide-answer:2","parentItemId":"b23c3ff2-fc70-5fb5-8da8-8f909c7bc704","revision":1,"payload":{"body":"V = 1,200,000(0.8)^t < 400,000 gives (0.8)^t < 1/3. Take logs: t ln 0.8 < −ln 3. Since ln 0.8 is negative, dividing flips the sign: t > ln 3/(−ln 0.8) = 1.0986/0.2231 = 4.92. So the value first falls below ₦400,000 after 5 years. Check: after 4 years V = ₦491,520; after 5 years V = ₦393,216."}},{"itemId":"282ef8b5-d965-50d6-bb62-82ecee2cb0a0","courseId":"e6ebc3e3-e990-5459-84af-06a4f05aea89","kind":"model_answer","questionId":null,"sourceKey":"guide-answer:3","parentItemId":"b0c82034-aee8-554d-9d28-7486f0bf2628","revision":1,"payload":{"body":"• (a) MC = C'(x) = x + 20; at 40, MC = ₦60.\n• (b) C(41) − C(40) = (840.5 + 820 + 800) − (800 + 800 + 800) = 2,460.5 − 2,400 = ₦60.50.\n• (c) AC = C/x = 0.5x + 20 + 800/x = 20 + 20 + 20 = ₦60.\n• (d) d(AC)/dx = 0.5 − 800/x^2 = 0 gives x^2 = 1,600, x = 40; d^2(AC)/dx^2 = 1,600/x^3 > 0, so this is a minimum. Check: at x = 40, MC = AC = ₦60, as the rule says."}},{"itemId":"b9831ff1-0289-510b-ae02-60228db0fd80","courseId":"e6ebc3e3-e990-5459-84af-06a4f05aea89","kind":"model_answer","questionId":null,"sourceKey":"guide-answer:4","parentItemId":"30170638-cfef-567e-beeb-18d16565546f","revision":1,"payload":{"body":"f_x = 4x − 4 = 0, so x = 1. f_y = 2y + 6 = 0, so y = −3. f_xx = 4, f_yy = 2, f_xy = 0, D = 4 × 2 − 0 = 8 > 0 and f_xx > 0: relative minimum at (1, −3). f(1, −3) = 2 + 9 − 4 − 18 + 15 = 4."}},{"itemId":"c02a154d-0130-5d6a-817e-8fd0902f3b69","courseId":"e6ebc3e3-e990-5459-84af-06a4f05aea89","kind":"model_answer","questionId":null,"sourceKey":"guide-answer:5","parentItemId":"76ac660f-1f2c-50b9-af24-01aed5ad3cc2","revision":1,"payload":{"body":"Contribution per shirt = 1,500 − 900 = ₦600. Break-even q = 240,000/600 = 400 shirts. Break-even revenue = 1,500 × 400 = ₦600,000. Profit on 500 = 600 × 500 − 240,000 = ₦60,000."}},{"itemId":"e728448d-5d07-5b6c-9062-99cb6bd939bb","courseId":"e6ebc3e3-e990-5459-84af-06a4f05aea89","kind":"model_answer","questionId":null,"sourceKey":"guide-answer:6","parentItemId":"09721817-1dac-5dce-8e8d-9bf794e1016b","revision":1,"payload":{"body":"i = 0.06/12 = 0.005; n = 5 × 12 = 60. (1.005)^(−60) = 0.741372, so 1 − 0.741372 = 0.258628. R = Pi/[1 − (1 + i)^(−n)] = 100,000 × 0.005/0.258628 = 500/0.258628 = ₦1,933.28. Total paid = 60 × 1,933.28 = ₦115,996.81 (unrounded R); interest = 115,996.81 − 100,000 = ₦15,997 (nearest naira)."}},{"itemId":"d646ce0f-ce89-59d1-a2b5-6c47f7a8a655","courseId":"e6ebc3e3-e990-5459-84af-06a4f05aea89","kind":"model_answer","questionId":null,"sourceKey":"guide-answer:7","parentItemId":"9d97860a-e6b4-5238-930a-9a2bfe32f3be","revision":1,"payload":{"body":"D = 2(8) − 5(3) = 16 − 15 = 1. Dx = 24(8) − 5(38) = 192 − 190 = 2. Dy = 2(38) − 24(3) = 76 − 72 = 4. x = Dx/D = 2, y = Dy/D = 4. Check: 2(2) + 5(4) = 24 and 3(2) + 8(4) = 38."}},{"itemId":"1ea283fc-9c97-5b62-8cdf-ca3f86559a1d","courseId":"e6ebc3e3-e990-5459-84af-06a4f05aea89","kind":"model_answer","questionId":null,"sourceKey":"guide-answer:8","parentItemId":"da4f50e2-430a-554d-963f-b76a46c4bd58","revision":1,"payload":{"body":"ar² = 18 and ar⁵ = 486. Divide: r³ = 486/18 = 27, so r = 3. Then a = 18/9 = 2. S_5 = a(r^5 − 1)/(r − 1) = 2(243 − 1)/2 = 242. Check: 2 + 6 + 18 + 54 + 162 = 242."}},{"itemId":"01c7a0e0-ec6d-553a-908a-08fe0dc1c493","courseId":"e6ebc3e3-e990-5459-84af-06a4f05aea89","kind":"model_answer","questionId":null,"sourceKey":"guide-answer:9","parentItemId":"32f8ea69-0d56-5fd0-a451-38fc24d6aa63","revision":1,"payload":{"body":"n(R ∪ B) = 120 + 90 − 30 = 180. Neither = 200 − 180 = 20. Rice only = 120 − 30 = 90; beans only = 90 − 30 = 60; exactly one = 90 + 60 = 150 (check: 180 − 30 = 150)."}}]$expected_content$::jsonb,
  'mathematics-business: model_answer published payload and identity match source');
