  'payload', payload) order by source_key collate "C"), '[]'::jsonb)
  from public.read_published_managed_content('caf0ea5d-6cc0-5bd0-8719-c6f1a95ceec1')
  where kind = 'model_answer') = $expected_content$[{"itemId":"cd022cc0-bfb4-5740-9a65-e86f5ef9209e","courseId":"caf0ea5d-6cc0-5bd0-8719-c6f1a95ceec1","kind":"model_answer","questionId":null,"sourceKey":"guide-answer:1","parentItemId":"e310cac9-bb61-5215-81d6-0a503d9c8621","revision":1,"payload":{"body":"• Year 1: 8 / 1.12 = ₦7.1429m.\n• Year 2: 9 / 1.12^2 = 9 / 1.2544 = ₦7.1747m.\n• Year 3: 10 / 1.12^3 = 10 / 1.404928 = ₦7.1178m.\n• Value = 7.1429 + 7.1747 + 7.1178 = ₦21.44m (rounded to 2 d.p.), well below the undiscounted ₦27m."}},{"itemId":"79695942-a7dd-5cb7-a2d9-fd732b74dedd","courseId":"caf0ea5d-6cc0-5bd0-8719-c6f1a95ceec1","kind":"model_answer","questionId":null,"sourceKey":"guide-answer:2","parentItemId":"05c9ca48-cb8f-5ac6-a10d-bd84f49d7fe2","revision":1,"payload":{"body":"• Accounting profit = 10,000,000 − 6,500,000 = ₦3,500,000.\n• Implicit costs = 1,500,000 + (4,000,000 × 0.12 = 480,000) = ₦1,980,000.\n• Economic profit = 3,500,000 − 1,980,000 = ₦1,520,000, an above-normal profit: catering beats her best alternative."}},{"itemId":"6a0bceb7-ee10-5f73-976c-05bd972459a1","courseId":"caf0ea5d-6cc0-5bd0-8719-c6f1a95ceec1","kind":"model_answer","questionId":null,"sourceKey":"guide-answer:3","parentItemId":"4bd3c121-03a7-5136-8083-ef24dea93d88","revision":1,"payload":{"body":"• %ΔQ = (300 - 200) / [(200 + 300)/2] = 100 / 250 = 40%.\n• %ΔP = (400 - 500) / [(500 + 400)/2] = -100 / 450 = -22.22%.\n• PED = 40 / 22.22 = 1.8 in absolute value: elastic.\n• TR before = ₦500 x 200 = ₦100,000; TR after = ₦400 x 300 = ₦120,000. Revenue rose by ₦20,000, as expected when price is cut on elastic demand."}},{"itemId":"fa504d69-82e5-5472-80e3-3bcdb772b02e","courseId":"caf0ea5d-6cc0-5bd0-8719-c6f1a95ceec1","kind":"model_answer","questionId":null,"sourceKey":"guide-answer:4","parentItemId":"ef914fd9-9610-5ce7-b1de-3f701eff4930","revision":1,"payload":{"body":"Moving average uses weeks 2 to 5: (64 + 70 + 66 + 72) / 4 = 272 / 4 = 68.00 bags. Exponential smoothing: F6 = 68 + 0.5 x (72 - 68) = 68 + 2 = 70 bags. The smoothing forecast is higher because it gives half the weight to the latest (high) week."}},{"itemId":"16019f53-9e16-5e7d-9f40-0810c41cea93","courseId":"caf0ea5d-6cc0-5bd0-8719-c6f1a95ceec1","kind":"model_answer","questionId":null,"sourceKey":"guide-answer:5","parentItemId":"00a2f083-5476-5812-9189-babd4a5c029c","revision":1,"payload":{"body":"Q | TVC (₦) | AVC = TVC/Q (₦) | ATC = (200 + TVC)/Q (₦) | MC (₦)\n1 | 80 | 80 | 280 | 80\n2 | 140 | 70 | 170 | 60\n3 | 210 | 70 | 136.67 | 70\n4 | 320 | 80 | 130 | 110\n(ATC at 3 rounded to 2 decimal places.) Minimum AVC is ₦70 (at 2 and 3 units), so the shut-down price is ₦70: below it, revenue would not cover variable cost. Note that MC of the 3rd unit (₦70) equals AVC at its minimum."}},{"itemId":"d7d0ec6f-fd38-5a62-8321-ffa9004bc8dc","courseId":"caf0ea5d-6cc0-5bd0-8719-c6f1a95ceec1","kind":"model_answer","questionId":null,"sourceKey":"guide-answer:6","parentItemId":"676cac5a-37f5-5f0d-a8da-ac1420773b8b","revision":1,"payload":{"body":"A buyers = 30,000 x 0.20 = 6,000; value = 6,000 x ₦4,000 = ₦24,000,000. B buyers = 8,000 x 0.50 = 4,000; value = 4,000 x ₦5,000 = ₦20,000,000. Segment A is worth more, so a firm with limited resources serving only A is using concentrated (niche) marketing."}},{"itemId":"de6b39e2-ae09-5232-b202-abe5c57469fd","courseId":"caf0ea5d-6cc0-5bd0-8719-c6f1a95ceec1","kind":"model_answer","questionId":null,"sourceKey":"guide-answer:7","parentItemId":"060f6630-377b-5ee1-a865-be44efa268f4","revision":1,"payload":{"body":"(1) A Plc can invite the general public to buy its shares; an Ltd cannot. (2) An Ltd restricts the transfer of its shares; a Plc's shares are freely transferable and may be listed on the Nigerian Exchange. (3) Under CAMA 2020 an Ltd has 1 to 50 members, while a Plc needs at least 2 and has no maximum; a Plc must also publish more financial information. Shared feature: both give shareholders limited liability (and both are separate legal entities with perpetual succession, registered by the CAC)."}},{"itemId":"fa46f1e0-5a0c-5e33-bf72-212283d8d86d","courseId":"caf0ea5d-6cc0-5bd0-8719-c6f1a95ceec1","kind":"model_answer","questionId":null,"sourceKey":"guide-answer:8","parentItemId":"5d65ec8b-d2fe-516b-8e5e-90e1b712669f","revision":1,"payload":{"body":"Loss = (P − ATC) × Q = (250 − 290) × 800 = −₦32,000. Since P (₦250) is above AVC (₦230), it should keep producing. If it shut down it would lose its whole fixed cost: AFC = 290 − 230 = ₦60, so FC = 60 × 800 = ₦48,000. Producing keeps the loss ₦16,000 smaller."}}]$expected_content$::jsonb,
  'managerial-economics: model_answer published payload and identity match source');
